API-17: return the halt flag from EN_gettimeparam(EN_HALTFLAG)

The EN_QTIME case had no break and fell through into an empty
EN_HALTFLAG case, so EN_HALTFLAG always returned 0 (and EN_QTIME only
worked because the empty case ends with a break). Add the break and
return hyd->Haltflag, which runhyd() sets when an unbalanced solution
halts the run (UNBALANCED STOP).

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply API-17_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/epanet.c b/src/epanet.c
index 47dc1e4..ef20814 100644
--- a/src/epanet.c
+++ b/src/epanet.c
@@ -1621,7 +1621,9 @@ int DLLEXPORT EN_gettimeparam(EN_Project p, int param, long *value)
         break;
     case EN_QTIME:
         *value = time->Qtime;
+        break;
     case EN_HALTFLAG:
+        *value = p->hydraul.Haltflag;
         break;
     case EN_NEXTEVENT:
         *value = time->Hstep; // find the lesser of the hydraulic time step length,
